<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Muhammad Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Hafs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1221</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Muhammad Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Hafs was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> and a son of Abu Hafs Umar, a companion of the Almohad founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a>. Appointed in 1207, he governed the province from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> with wide autonomy until his death in 1221. His son Abu Zakariya Yahya broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in 1229, founding the independent Hafsid state.</p></div>
